---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About">
  <article class="essay">
    <header>
      <p class="kicker">About</p>
      <h1>From the point of sale to the control plane</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I started in hospitality IT, keeping Oracle Simphony point-of-sale terminals and Opera
        property-management systems alive in restaurants and hotels, where an outage is measured in
        tables that can't close a check. That job taught me the thing I still care about most:
        the system has to work on a Friday night, not just in the demo.
      </p>
      <p>
        Today I'm a cloud engineer at Circa Las Vegas, working on the Azure Kubernetes Service
        platform behind a mobile sportsbook. Outside work I run THALES, a private cloud built
        to satisfy the five NIST characteristics of cloud computing, operated by one person.
        It runs Talos Linux, Flux, Cilium, Ceph, Vault and Authentik, and it is where I learn
        things before I need them.
      </p>
      <h2>The other half</h2>
      <p>
        In college I studied the history of ideas — seventeenth-century England, the Scottish and
        French Enlightenment, Diderot and the encyclopedists. It shows up in the work more than
        you might expect. Every host in THALES is named for a Classical Greek thinker, and my
        habits of mind are Hume's: suspicious of foundations, interested in what actually
        happens rather than what a system claims about itself.
      </p>
      <blockquote>A config line existing is not a config line working.</blockquote>
      <p>
        When I'm not at a terminal I'm usually playing guitar.
      </p>
      <h2>Colophon</h2>
      <p>
        This site is a static Astro build served by unprivileged nginx. Jenkins builds the image
        with Kaniko, Trivy blocks anything with a critical CVE, and Flux rolls it into a staging
        namespace, where Flagger runs a blue/green analysis before the new version takes traffic.
        Production gets the same image only after it has passed there. The site it replaced — PHP,
        MariaDB and a lot of green-on-black — is preserved at <a href="https://testing.jasonharker.com">testing.jasonharker.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
